From: Project Luma <maintainers@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] shell: restore status island material ownership

The quick-settings actor is not a child inside the separate status material:
it is the material actor itself.  It therefore carries luma-shelf-material,
luma-status-cluster, and the effective luma-surface-* class on one actor.

The generic status rules deliberately make an inner status cluster
transparent, but their descendant selectors do not express this same-actor
ownership.  Depending on theme cascade and state, the separate status island
could consequently retain only its stroke while the wallpaper painted through
its entire body.  The dock did not share the status-cluster class and remained
filled, leaving the two sibling islands visibly inconsistent.

Name the real owner explicitly in separate mode for all four treatments.
Connected mode still clears that actor because the common Shelf surface is the
single material owner there.

---
 data/theme/luma-shelf.css | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/data/theme/luma-shelf.css b/data/theme/luma-shelf.css
--- a/data/theme/luma-shelf.css
+++ b/data/theme/luma-shelf.css
@@ -417,5 +417,31 @@
 .luma-surface-glass .luma-status-cluster:hover,
 .luma-surface-glass .luma-status-cluster:active { background-color: transparent; }
+
+/* In separate mode the quick-settings/status actor is the island's material
+ * owner, not a child inside another material. Match those co-located roles so
+ * the material fill cannot be erased by generic panel-button/status rules. */
+.luma-shelf-root.luma-shelf-separate > .luma-shelf-group >
+.luma-shelf-actions-island >
+.luma-shelf-material.luma-status-cluster.luma-surface-light {
+  background-color: #f1f2f3; }
+.luma-shelf-root.luma-shelf-separate > .luma-shelf-group >
+.luma-shelf-actions-island >
+.luma-shelf-material.luma-status-cluster.luma-surface-dark {
+  background-color: #21252b; }
+.luma-shelf-root.luma-shelf-separate > .luma-shelf-group >
+.luma-shelf-actions-island >
+.luma-shelf-material.luma-status-cluster.luma-surface-frost {
+  background-color: rgba(241, 242, 243, 0.73); }
+.luma-shelf-root.luma-shelf-separate > .luma-shelf-group >
+.luma-shelf-actions-island >
+.luma-shelf-material.luma-status-cluster.luma-surface-glass {
+  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.31); }
+
+/* Connected mode owns one material on the outer Shelf surface. */
+.luma-shelf-root.luma-shelf-connected > .luma-shelf-group >
+.luma-shelf-actions-island >
+.luma-shelf-material.luma-status-cluster {
+  background-color: transparent; }
 .luma-surface-light .luma-status-hover,
 .luma-surface-frost .luma-status-hover { background-color: rgba(25,27,31,0.14); }
 .luma-surface-dark .luma-status-hover,
-- 
